  "description": "End-to-end playbook for working a GitHub issue (or bug-fix PR) on nubjs/nub: triage → acknowledge an external report with an \"Investigating\" comment → reproduce it yourself → SIZE it → fix it at that size (most issues are a small fix you just write — no investigation spike, no sub-agent fleet, no top-tier model) → open a PR that references the issue with `Closes #N` → on merge, comment the resolution → on release, comment the version + release link. Invoke (via the Skill tool) whenever you pick up an issue to work, or are asked to fix a reported bug. Encodes both the maintainer-hygiene conventions in AGENTS.md (so the reporter is acknowledged, the issue auto-closes on merge, and the loop closes when the fix ships) and the proportionality gate that keeps an ordinary bug from being worked like an audit.",
